      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0ce72f90-5acc-58a0-8d33-91036bbded9b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Apple Dumpling Gang; Something Wicked This Way Comes; The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again; The Shaggy D.A.; The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh; The Fox and the Hound\n- People: Buddy Baker; Bill Bixby; Jack Clayton; Ray Bradbury; Paul J. Smith\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Concepts: California Gold Rush\n\nFacts:\n- Buddy Baker was an American composer who lived from January 4, 1918, to July 26, 2002.\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang is about slick gambler Russell Donovan, played by Bill Bixby, who is duped into caring for orphans who later strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- Buddy Baker and Paul J. Smith scored the Disney film The Apple Dumpling Gang in 1975.\n- Buddy Baker scored The Shaggy D.A. in 1976 and The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh in 1977.\n- Buddy Baker scored The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again in 1979 and The Fox and the Hound in 1981.\n- Something Wicked This Way Comes is a 1983 American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton and produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- Something Wicked This Way Comes was adapted from Ray Bradbury's novel of the same name using a screenplay written by Bradbury.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ce993e7a-c132-5203-a126-d45b7be5629c",
        "text": "Page: The Apple Dumpling Gang (film). Sentence: The Apple Dumpling Gang is a 1975 American comedy-western film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a slick gambler named Russell Donovan (Bill Bixby) who is duped into taking care of a group of orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\nPage: Something Wicked This Way Comes (film). Sentence: Something Wicked This Way Comes is a 1983 American horror fantasy film directed by Jack Clayton and produced by Walt Disney Productions from a screenplay written by Ray Bradbury, based on his novel of the same name.\nPage: Buddy Baker (composer). Sentence: Norman Dale \"Buddy\" Baker (January 4, 1918 – July 26, 2002) was an American composer who, together with Paul J. Smith, scored many Disney films, such as \"The Apple Dumpling Gang\" in 1975, \"The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again\" in 1979, \"The Shaggy D.A.\" in 1976, \"The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh\" in 1977, and \"The Fox and the Hound\" in 1981.",
